##1461. Check If a String Contains All Binary Codes of size K
##LeetCode link: https://leetcode.com/problems/check-if-a-string-contains-all-binary-codes-of-size-k/?envType=daily-question&envId=2026-02-23

##Approach:
We slide a window of size k over the binary string and collect all substrings of length k in a Set to keep them unique.
There are exactly 2^k possible binary codes of length k.
If the number of unique substrings we found equals 2^k, then the string contains every possible binary code.
The intuition is counting: instead of generating all codes, we just check how many distinct ones appear.
If even one code is missing, the set size will be less than 2^k.

/**
 * @param {string} s
 * @param {number} k
 * @return {boolean}
 */
var hasAllCodes = function(s, k) {
    let set=new Set();
    for(let i=0;i<=s.length-k;i++){
        let sub=s.substring(i,i+k);
        set.add(sub);
        //console.log(sub);
        //console.log(sub.length);
    }
    let x=Math.pow(2,k);
    console.log(x);
    if(set.size===x)return true;
    else return false;
};
